// CouchDB, comprehensively: the pilot "comprehensive" suite of
// servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers (the README's "Pattern
// for comprehensive suites" says what later suites copy from it).
//
// Two describe blocks, two sets of tapes:
//
// 1. "modules/couchdb": ported from testcontainers-go
//    modules/couchdb/couchdb_test.go, by way of testcontainers-ae. It tests
//    the MODULE (default and custom admin credentials, the connection
//    string), one container per case, Basic auth.
//
// 2. "CouchDB HTTP API": written for servirtium-vcr. Re-usable recordings
//    of CouchDB's HTTP API, one tape per scenario, for any language's tests
//    to replay with no CouchDB. This is the comprehensive part.
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes
// are the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test
// framework that makes the same requests, in the same order, against a
// Servirtium replay server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things.
// Any Servirtium implementation replays them. Every request here is plain
// HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Content-Type: application/json   (only when there is a body; text/plain
//                                     for the attachment upload)
//   Cookie: AuthSession=...          (the logged-in cases only, see below)
//   Accept: application/json         (one request, ?attachments=true)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as
// encoded here), the recorded request headers and the body (byte for byte:
// send the JSON bodies exactly as written in this file, no spaces), and fails
// a case whose recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and
// Content-Length are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
//
// PORTING, the tape for each case: <case>.md beside this file, where <case>
// is the second argument of servirtium.recording(...) in that case. The
// cases are independent: each makes its own database (a fixed name, created
// with ?q=1, below), works in it, and deletes it on the tape, so any one tape
// replays alone and in any order.
//
// Login, and "already logged in"
// ------------------------------
// Logging in gets ONE tape of its own, logs_in_and_out_with_a_session_cookie
// (POST /_session with a right and a wrong password, GET /_session before and
// after, DELETE /_session). Every other API case is ALREADY LOGGED IN: each
// request carries the session cookie CouchDB issues at POST /_session,
//   Cookie: AuthSession=<opaque value>
// and the login itself is not on that case's tape. When recording, the test
// logs in directly against the container, outside the recorder (login_live
// below), so the cookie is real; one case refuses_a_client_that_has_not_
// logged_in shows what happens without it. These are component-level tests
// of CouchDB's API, not full-stack ones: the tapes stand in for CouchDB.
//
// PORTING, getting into the logged-in state without the login tape: send
// any `Cookie: AuthSession=<anything>` header on every request. The tapes
// hold the cookie as `Cookie: AuthSession=COOKIE_1` (Servirtium's
// redact_credentials preset), and playback matches a credential header on
// PRESENCE, not value: present, it matches; missing, it does not. Against a
// live CouchDB, log in first (POST /_session {"name":..,"password":..}, take
// AuthSession=<value> from the Set-Cookie response header) or send
// `Authorization: Basic ...` instead (CouchDB accepts both, but the tapes
// recorded a Cookie, so replay wants a Cookie). A port's
// "is-already-logged-in" fixture is just that header; to test the login
// itself, replay the login tape, or both tapes one after the other. A
// consequence of presence matching: a replay cannot tell a valid cookie
// from a forged one, so the unauthorized case sends no cookie at all.
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them all and
// the interactions each touched ("none" where it did not). In short:
//   - normalized (each distinct value a stable {{name-N}} token, the same
//     token wherever it recurs, because a client sends it back): sequence
//     ids ({{seq-N}}: update_seq, last_seq, a change's seq, since=... in a
//     later request) and bare 32-hex uuids ({{uuid-N}}: the server uuid,
//     /_uuids, server-generated document ids, in later paths too), and the
//     ETags computed over those ({{etag-N}}: a client may send one back as
//     If-None-Match).
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): a database's
//     instance_start_time, and the session cookie's Expires date.
//   - redacted: the session cookie (COOKIE_N, matched on presence), and the
//     password in the login body ("password":"REDACTED[admin]" and
//     "REDACTED[admin-wrong-password]", put back on replay, so the wrong
//     password stays told apart from the right one).
//   - left out: X-Couch-Request-ID and X-CouchDB-Body-Time response headers
//     (and Date, as everywhere).
//
// PORTING: in playback, a normalized or redacted value comes back as its
// token, verbatim: the server uuid is "{{uuid-1}}", a last_seq is
// "{{seq-2}}", the cookie is AuthSession=COOKIE_1. Treat every id, seq and
// ETag as an opaque string (never assert its length or shape) and send it
// back exactly as received; the tape expects the token in the later request,
// e.g. `GET /tcae_ids/{{uuid-2}}` and `GET .../_changes?since={{seq-2}}`.
// Send the braces as they are: playback compares paths byte for byte, so a
// client that percent-encodes `{` as %7B will not match. Also: CouchDB
// separates the rows of view, _find and _changes results with CRLF; the
// tapes keep the CRs, but Servirtium's playback folds a tape's CRLF to LF
// when it reads it, so replayed rows are LF-separated. Parse the JSON, or
// ignore CRs, rather than comparing those bodies byte for byte.
//
// Revisions are NOT rewritten. A _rev is "<generation>-<md5 of the body,
// the previous rev and the deleted flag>", so the same writes give the same
// revs on every run: {"v":1} written fresh is always
// "1-7a7e4b29f3af401e69b6f86e4c26b727", whatever the document's id (the id
// is not hashed: a, b and c in follows_the_changes_feed_with_since share
// it). Use them in assertions if you like; a document's ETag is its rev.
// Attachment digests and ETags (base64 MD5 of the bytes) and Mango bookmarks
// are deterministic too. The ETags that are not (computed over sequence ids
// or uuids) are normalized, below.
//
// Every database is created with ?q=1 (one shard; CouchDB 3's default is
// 2). With two shards, _changes interleaves the shards' feeds in an order
// that can differ run to run; with one, the order is the order of the writes.
// A port replaying the tapes need not care: the requests are on the tape.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: server info (/, /_up, /_all_dbs, /_uuids, /_session); database
// create / info / _security / delete; document CRUD with revisions, old
// revisions and revs_info; 409 on a stale revision; replication-style
// conflicts (new_edits=false, ?conflicts=true, resolving); _bulk_docs
// (create, update with a per-document conflict, delete); _all_docs with
// include_docs, key, keys, startkey/endkey, limit/skip and descending;
// attachments standalone (PUT/GET/DELETE) and inline (base64 in the
// document, ?attachments=true); design documents with map and map/reduce
// views (_count, _sum, group, reduce=false, key, range, include_docs, keys);
// Mango (_index create/list/delete, _find with and without an index, sort,
// fields, limit, the bookmark); _changes (normal feed, since=, limit,
// include_docs, a deletion); server-generated ids; login and logout; and the
// representative errors 400, 401, 404, 409 and 412 (405 too).
// Out: continuous / longpoll / eventsource feeds (connection- and
// timing-level: Servirtium records messages, not connections); replication
// and the scheduler (asynchronous, timing-dependent); compaction,
// _active_tasks, _node stats and config (node-specific, varying numbers);
// users other than the admin, and roles; partitioned databases; _purge;
// show/list/update functions (deprecated in CouchDB 3, gone in 4); full-text
// search (needs Clouseau, not in the image). Each could be a later case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test couchdb/test_couchdb.ae                    container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test couchdb/test_couchdb.ae  write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test couchdb/test_couchdb.ae  fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test couchdb/test_couchdb.ae  no container: the tapes
// The API cases share one container (started on the first one and removed at
// the end); the module cases each start their own.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.encoding
import std.json
import std.http.client
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.couchdb

const IMAGE = "couchdb:3"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would: Go's net/http adds `Go-http-client/1.1` by itself, Aether's
// std.http.client adds none. Set here, in the test's own client, so the
// recordings show a representative request; Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// The cookie the logged-in cases send in playback, where there is no CouchDB
// to log in to. Any value does: the tapes match the Cookie header on
// presence (see "already logged in" above).
const PLAYBACK_COOKIE = "AuthSession=any-value-replay-matches-on-presence"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Response headers of the last request that some cases look at.
var last_set_cookie: string = ""
var last_etag: string = ""
var last_content_type: string = ""

// One HTTP request: (status, body, error). hdrs are "Name: value" lines;
// ctype is the body's Content-Type (none when the body is empty).
fn http_send(method: string, url: string, hdrs: string[], ctype: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
    for h in hdrs {
        colon = string.index_of(h, ":")
        client.set_header(req, string.substring(h, 0, colon), string.trim(string.substring(h, colon + 1, string.length(h))))
    }
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), ctype) }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    last_set_cookie = client.response_header(r, "Set-Cookie")
    last_etag = client.response_header(r, "ETag")
    last_content_type = client.response_header(r, "Content-Type")
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b, ""
}

// The module cases' requests (Basic auth or none).
fn http_do(method: string, url: string, hdrs: string[], body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    return http_send(method, url, hdrs, "application/json", body)
}

fn basic(user: string, pw: string) -> string {
    return "Authorization: Basic ${encoding.base64_encode_padded(string.bytes("${user}:${pw}"))}"
}

// A recording shows "Authorization: Basic REDACTED[<label>]"; playback still
// matches the real header. Not Servirtium's redact_credentials preset: that
// matches Authorization on presence, and these cases tell a right password
// from a wrong one, which playback should keep checking.
fn redact_basic(user: string, pw: string, label: string) {
    secret = encoding.base64_encode_padded(string.bytes("${user}:${pw}"))
    servirtium.redact(servirtium.FIELD_REQUEST_HEADERS, "Basic ${secret}", "Basic REDACTED[${label}]")
}

// The API cases: the base URL of the current recording and the session
// cookie ("AuthSession=...") every logged-in request carries.
var api: string = ""
var cookie: string = ""

// A logged-in request with a JSON body (or none): (status, body). A transport
// error fails the case.
fn couch(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    return couch_typed(method, path, "application/json", body)
}

fn couch_typed(method: string, path: string, ctype: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}", ["Cookie: ${cookie}"], ctype, body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A logged-in GET that asks for JSON (Accept: application/json), where
// CouchDB would otherwise choose another representation.
fn couch_json(path: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send("GET", "${api}${path}", ["Cookie: ${cookie}", "Accept: application/json"], "", "")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "GET ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A request with no credentials at all: (status, body).
fn anonymous(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}", [], "application/json", body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// Percent-encode a query-string value (a JSON key such as "apple" goes on
// the wire as %22apple%22): RFC 3986 unreserved bytes stay, the rest %XX.
fn q(s: string) -> string {
    hex = "0123456789ABCDEF"
    out = ""
    b = string.bytes(s)
    i = 0
    while i < b.len {
        ch = b[i]
        keep = (ch >= 48 && ch <= 57) || (ch >= 65 && ch <= 90) || (ch >= 97 && ch <= 122) || ch == 45 || ch == 46 || ch == 95 || ch == 126
        if keep {
            out = string.concat(out, string.substring(s, i, i + 1))
        } else {
            hi = string.substring(hex, (ch >> 4) & 15, ((ch >> 4) & 15) + 1)
            lo = string.substring(hex, ch & 15, (ch & 15) + 1)
            out = "${out}%${hi}${lo}"
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return out
}

// The body with its carriage returns removed. CouchDB streams view, _find
// and _changes results with CRLF between rows; the tape keeps the CRs, but
// Servirtium's playback reads a tape with CRLF folded to LF (so a tape
// checked out with autocrlf still parses), so on replay the rows are
// LF-separated. Assert on lf(body) and both pass.
fn lf(body: string) -> string {
    return string.replace_all(body, "\r", "")
}

// A JSON string key for the query string: qk("b") is "b" encoded, %22b%22.
fn qk(s: string) -> string {
    return q("\"${s}\"")
}

// A string in a JSON body by a dotted path ("rev", "uuids.0", "docs.1._id");
// "" when absent or not a string.
fn jstr(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    doc, err = json.parse(body)
    if err != "" { return "" }
    let v: ptr = doc
    rest = path
    while string.length(rest) > 0 && v != null {
        p = rest
        dot = string.index_of(rest, ".")
        if dot >= 0 {
            p = string.substring(rest, 0, dot)
            rest = string.substring(rest, dot + 1, string.length(rest))
        } else {
            rest = ""
        }
        if json.json_type(v) == json.JSON_ARRAY {
            idx, _ = string.to_int(p)
            a, _ = json.array_get(v, idx)
            v = a
        } else {
            o, _ = json.object_get(v, p)
            v = o
        }
    }
    out = ""
    if v != null {
        s, serr = json.get_string(v)
        if serr == "" { out = string.copy(s) }
    }
    json.free(doc)
    return out
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live container the API cases share (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var shared_addr: string = ""
var shared_container: ptr = null

// The shared container's base URL, starting it on first use ("" on failure).
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_addr) > 0 { return shared_addr }
    db, err = couchdb.run(IMAGE)
    if db == null {
        spec.fail("couchdb starts: ${err}")
        return ""
    }
    shared_container = db.container as ptr
    spec.assert_ok(err, "couchdb starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    port, _ = tc.mapped_port(db.container, couchdb.PORT)
    shared_addr = "http://localhost:${port}"
    return shared_addr
}

// Log in directly against the container, outside any recording: the
// "AuthSession=..." cookie the logged-in cases carry.
fn login_live(addr: string) -> string {
    st, b, err = http_send("POST", "${addr}/_session", [], "application/json", "{\"name\":\"${couchdb.DEFAULT_USER}\",\"password\":\"${couchdb.DEFAULT_PASSWORD}\"}")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "log in (not recorded)")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "log in (not recorded): ${b}")
    semi = string.index_of(last_set_cookie, ";")
    if semi < 0 { return last_set_cookie }
    return string.substring(last_set_cookie, 0, semi)
}

// Start a logged-in API case: in a live mode, the shared container, a fresh
// session cookie and, should an earlier failed run have left it, the case's
// database removed (none of that is recorded); then the recording. Sets
// `api` and `cookie`; returns the recording handle, and ok = 0 when the case
// cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string, db: string) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    cookie = PLAYBACK_COOKIE
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        cookie = login_live(addr)
        if string.length(db) > 0 { http_send("DELETE", "${addr}/${db}", ["Cookie: ${cookie}"], "", "") }
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("couchdb", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// Create the case's database (one shard, see the header) and assert it.
fn create_db(db: string) {
    st, b = couch("PUT", "/${db}?q=1", "")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "PUT /${db} creates it: ${b}")
    spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"ok\":true}\n", "the body is {\"ok\":true}")
}

fn delete_db(db: string) {
    st, b = couch("DELETE", "/${db}", "")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "DELETE /${db}: ${b}")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The module cases' rules.
fn module_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // Every Basic credential the cases send is kept off the tapes.
    redact_basic("admin", "password", "admin")
    redact_basic("admin", "nope", "admin-wrong-password")
    redact_basic("testuser", "testpassword", "testuser")
    redact_basic("us er", "p@ss/w:rd", "percent-encoded-user")
    // What differs run to run: the per-request id and timing headers, the
    // server's uuid, a database's start time and its opaque sequence tokens.
    servirtium.remove_header(servirtium.FIELD_RESPONSE_HEADERS, "X-Couch-Request-ID")
    servirtium.remove_header(servirtium.FIELD_RESPONSE_HEADERS, "X-CouchDB-Body-Time")
    servirtium.normalize("[0-9a-f]{32}", "couchdb-uuid")
    // (instance_start_time only: a bare 10-digit pattern also hit the
    // X-Couch-Request-ID header when its ten hex digits happened to be all
    // decimal, so the rules footer differed between runs.)
    servirtium.collapse("\"instance_start_time\":\"[0-9]+\"", "\"instance_start_time\":\"946684800\"")
    servirtium.collapse("_seq\":\"[0-9]+-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\"", "_seq\":\"0-SEQ\"")
}

// The API cases' rules. Rules apply to every recording after them, so the
// two blocks each clear and register their own.
fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // A request id and a body timing on every response: noise.
    servirtium.remove_header(servirtium.FIELD_RESPONSE_HEADERS, "X-Couch-Request-ID")
    servirtium.remove_header(servirtium.FIELD_RESPONSE_HEADERS, "X-CouchDB-Body-Time")
    // The session cookie, in Set-Cookie (login tape) and Cookie (every
    // logged-in request): Servirtium's credential preset writes each
    // distinct value as COOKIE_N and replays the header on presence. (It
    // covers Authorization too; these cases send none.)
    servirtium.redact_credentials()
    // The password in the login body. Labelled literal redactions, not a
    // collapse: playback puts the real text back before comparing, so the
    // replay still tells the right password from the wrong one. (A
    // placeholder must not contain another, hence the brackets.)
    servirtium.redact(servirtium.FIELD_REQUEST_BODY, "\"password\":\"${couchdb.DEFAULT_PASSWORD}\"", "\"password\":\"REDACTED[admin]\"")
    servirtium.redact(servirtium.FIELD_REQUEST_BODY, "\"password\":\"not-the-password\"", "\"password\":\"REDACTED[admin-wrong-password]\"")
    // Set-Cookie's Expires is the login time plus ten minutes. Collapsed:
    // a client never sends it back.
    servirtium.collapse("Expires=[A-Z][a-z]{2}, [0-9]{2}-[A-Z][a-z]{2}-[0-9]{4} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2} GMT", "Expires=Sat, 01-Jan-2000 00:00:00 GMT")
    // When the database file was opened (Unix seconds, as a string). Only
    // in this field: a bare 10-digit pattern would also hit sizes and the
    // like.
    servirtium.collapse("\"instance_start_time\":\"[0-9]+\"", "\"instance_start_time\":\"946684800\"")
    // Sequence ids: "<number>-g1AAAA...", opaque, and different every run
    // (they embed the shard file's uuid). Normalized, not collapsed: a
    // client sends last_seq back as ?since=..., so the same value must be
    // the same token in the response and in the later request path. Revs
    // ("1-<hex>") never match: hex has no "g".
    servirtium.normalize("[0-9]+-g[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}", "seq")
    // Bare 32-hex uuids, in quotes: the server's uuid (GET /), /_uuids, and
    // the ids CouchDB gives documents POSTed without one, which come back
    // in a later request path (the token replaces the value there too).
    // The quotes keep revs out ("1-<32 hex>" has "1-" after the quote);
    // they are lookarounds, so the token replaces just the hex.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=\")[0-9a-f]{32}(?=\")", "uuid")
    // The ETag of a response built from those (_changes, /_uuids,
    // _all_dbs, the views after a write): an upper-case base-36 hash of
    // them, different every run. Normalized, since a client may send it
    // back as If-None-Match. A document's ETag is its rev ("1-<hex>") and
    // an attachment's the base64 MD5 of its bytes: both stable, neither
    // matches.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=ETag: \")[0-9A-Z]{20,30}(?=\")", "etag")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    module_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "modules/couchdb") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        spec.it("serves the welcome document and creates a database (TestCouchDB)") callback {
            addr = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                db, err = couchdb.run(IMAGE)
                if db != null { testing.cleanup_container(db.container) }
                spec.assert_ok(err, "couchdb starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                conn, cerr = couchdb.connection_string(db)
                spec.assert_ok(cerr, "connection string")
                spec.assert_contains(conn, "http://admin:password@", "default credentials in the URL")
                port, _ = tc.mapped_port(db.container, couchdb.PORT)
                spec.assert_str_eq(conn, "http://admin:password@localhost:${port}", "Go's format")
                addr = "http://localhost:${port}"
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("couchdb", "serves_the_welcome_document_and_creates_a_database", addr)
            auth = basic("admin", "password")
            st, body, herr = http_do("GET", "${base}/", [], "")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "GET /")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "welcome status")
            spec.assert_contains(body, "\"couchdb\":\"Welcome\"", "welcome document: ${body}")
            ust, _ub, uerr = http_do("GET", "${base}/_up", [], "")
            spec.assert_ok(uerr, "GET /_up")
            spec.assert_eq(ust, 200, "_up status")
            // no credentials: refused
            nst, _nb, nerr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/tcae_db", [], "")
            spec.assert_ok(nerr, "PUT without credentials")
            spec.assert_eq(nst, 401, "unauthenticated create is refused")
            // wrong credentials: refused
            wst, _wb, werr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/tcae_db", [basic("admin", "nope")], "")
            spec.assert_ok(werr, "PUT with wrong credentials")
            spec.assert_eq(wst, 401, "wrong password is refused")
            // the module's credentials: created
            pst, pbody, perr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/tcae_db", [auth], "")
            spec.assert_ok(perr, "PUT with the module's credentials")
            spec.assert_eq(pst, 201, "database created: ${pbody}")
            gst, gbody, gerr = http_do("GET", "${base}/tcae_db", [auth], "")
            spec.assert_ok(gerr, "GET database")
            spec.assert_eq(gst, 200, "database exists")
            spec.assert_contains(gbody, "\"db_name\":\"tcae_db\"", "its info: ${gbody}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("uses custom admin credentials (TestCouchDB_WithAdminCredentials)") callback {
            addr = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                db, err = couchdb.run(IMAGE) {
                    admin_credentials("testuser", "testpassword")
                }
                if db != null { testing.cleanup_container(db.container) }
                spec.assert_ok(err, "couchdb starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                conn, cerr = couchdb.connection_string(db)
                spec.assert_ok(cerr, "connection string")
                spec.assert_contains(conn, "http://testuser:testpassword@", "custom credentials in the URL")
                port, _ = tc.mapped_port(db.container, couchdb.PORT)
                addr = "http://localhost:${port}"
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("couchdb", "uses_custom_admin_credentials", addr)
            st, body, herr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/custom_db", [basic("testuser", "testpassword")], "")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "PUT")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "created with the custom credentials: ${body}")
            ost, _ob, oerr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/other_db", [basic("admin", "password")], "")
            spec.assert_ok(oerr, "PUT as the default admin")
            spec.assert_eq(ost, 401, "the default credentials no longer work")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("percent-encodes credentials in the connection string") callback {
            addr = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                db, err = couchdb.run(IMAGE) {
                    admin_credentials("us er", "p@ss/w:rd")
                }
                if db != null { testing.cleanup_container(db.container) }
                spec.assert_ok(err, "couchdb starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                conn, cerr = couchdb.connection_string(db)
                spec.assert_ok(cerr, "connection string")
                spec.assert_contains(conn, "http://us%20er:p%40ss%2Fw%3Ard@localhost:", "userinfo escaped")
                port, _ = tc.mapped_port(db.container, couchdb.PORT)
                addr = "http://localhost:${port}"
            }
            // (std.http.client refuses userinfo in a URL, so authenticate
            // with the same credentials in a header)
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("couchdb", "percent_encodes_credentials_in_the_connection_string", addr)
            st, body, herr = http_do("PUT", "${base}/enc_db", [basic("us er", "p@ss/w:rd")], "")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "PUT")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "the credentials the URL encodes authenticate: ${body}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "CouchDB HTTP API") {

        // ---- the login tape ----------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: the one tape with the login on it. No cookie on the first
        // request.
        //   GET    /_session                        -> 200, userCtx.name null (anonymous)
        //   POST   /_session {"name":"admin","password":<wrong>} -> 401
        //          {"error":"unauthorized","reason":"Name or password is incorrect."},
        //          and an EMPTY Set-Cookie: AuthSession=
        //   POST   /_session {"name":"admin","password":<right>} -> 200
        //          {"ok":true,"name":"admin","roles":["_admin"]},
        //          Set-Cookie: AuthSession=COOKIE_1; Version=1; Expires=...; Max-Age=600; Path=/; HttpOnly
        //   GET    /_session  Cookie: AuthSession=<from Set-Cookie> -> 200,
        //          userCtx admin, "authenticated":"cookie"
        //   DELETE /_session  Cookie: ... -> 200 {"ok":true}, Set-Cookie: AuthSession= (cleared)
        // The passwords are on the tape as REDACTED[admin] and
        // REDACTED[admin-wrong-password]; playback puts them back before
        // comparing, so a port sends the real test passwords ("password",
        // the module's default, and "not-the-password"). The cookie value is
        // COOKIE_1: take it from the replayed Set-Cookie, as a client would.
        // CouchDB's cookie is a signed timestamp, not a server-side session:
        // DELETE /_session tells the client to drop it, it does not revoke it.
        spec.it("logs in and out with a session cookie") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("logs_in_and_out_with_a_session_cookie", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "/_session", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_session: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"userCtx\":{\"name\":null,\"roles\":[]}", "nobody is logged in")

            st, b = anonymous("POST", "/_session", "{\"name\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"not-the-password\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 401, "a wrong password is refused: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"unauthorized\"", "unauthorized")

            st, b = anonymous("POST", "/_session", "{\"name\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"${couchdb.DEFAULT_PASSWORD}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the right password logs in: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"ok\":true,\"name\":\"admin\",\"roles\":[\"_admin\"]}\n", "the user and roles")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(last_set_cookie, "AuthSession=") == 1, "a session cookie: ${last_set_cookie}")
            spec.assert_contains(last_set_cookie, "HttpOnly", "HttpOnly")
            semi = string.index_of(last_set_cookie, ";")
            cookie = string.substring(last_set_cookie, 0, semi)

            st, b = couch("GET", "/_session", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_session with the cookie: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"userCtx\":{\"name\":\"admin\",\"roles\":[\"_admin\"]}", "logged in as admin")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"authenticated\":\"cookie\"", "by the cookie")

            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/_session", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "DELETE /_session logs out: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(last_set_cookie, "AuthSession=;") == 1, "the cookie is cleared: ${last_set_cookie}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: no credentials at all (no Cookie, no Authorization).
        //   GET /               -> 200 (the welcome document is public)
        //   GET /_all_dbs       -> 401 {"error":"unauthorized","reason":"You are not a server admin."}
        //   PUT /tcae_unauth?q=1 -> 401, same body
        //   GET /_session       -> 200, userCtx.name null
        // Not "a wrong cookie": replay matches a cookie on presence, so it
        // could not tell a forged cookie from a good one.
        spec.it("refuses a client that has not logged in") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("refuses_a_client_that_has_not_logged_in", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "/", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET / needs no login: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "/_all_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 401, "GET /_all_dbs needs a server admin: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"unauthorized\"", "unauthorized")
            st, b = anonymous("PUT", "/tcae_unauth?q=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 401, "creating a database needs a server admin: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "/_session", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_session: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"name\":null", "anonymous")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- already logged in from here on: every request carries the cookie

        // PORTING:
        //   GET /           -> 200 {"couchdb":"Welcome","version":..,"uuid":"{{uuid-1}}",..}
        //   GET /_up        -> 200 {"seeds":{},"status":"ok"}
        //   GET /_session   -> 200, userCtx admin, authenticated by cookie
        //                      (the check a port's logged-in fixture can make)
        //   GET /_uuids?count=3 -> 200 {"uuids":[3 x 32 hex]} ({{uuid-N}})
        spec.it("reports the server info") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_server_info", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = couch("GET", "/", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"couchdb\":\"Welcome\"", "the welcome document")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"vendor\":{\"name\":\"The Apache Software Foundation\"}", "the vendor")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/_up", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_up: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"status\":\"ok\"", "up")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/_session", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_session: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"userCtx\":{\"name\":\"admin\",\"roles\":[\"_admin\"]}", "already logged in as admin")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/_uuids?count=3", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_uuids: ${b}")
            // Not their length: on replay a normalized value comes back as its
            // token, "{{uuid-3}}". Treat ids as opaque strings.
            spec.assert_true(string.length(jstr(b, "uuids.2")) > 0, "three uuids")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: database lifecycle, in tcae_dbs.
        //   PUT    /tcae_dbs?q=1 -> 201 {"ok":true}, Location header
        //   PUT    /tcae_dbs?q=1 -> 412 {"error":"file_exists",..} (it exists)
        //   GET    /tcae_dbs     -> 200 info: db_name, doc_count 0, update_seq {{seq-N}},
        //                         instance_start_time collapsed, cluster.q 1
        //   GET    /_all_dbs     -> 200 ["tcae_dbs"]
        //   PUT    /tcae_dbs/_security {"admins":{..},"members":{"roles":["readers"]}} -> 200 {"ok":true}
        //   GET    /tcae_dbs/_security -> 200, the same object
        //   DELETE /tcae_dbs     -> 200 {"ok":true}
        //   GET    /tcae_dbs     -> 404 {"error":"not_found","reason":"Database does not exist."}
        //   DELETE /tcae_dbs     -> 404
        spec.it("creates, inspects and deletes a database") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_inspects_and_deletes_a_database", "tcae_dbs")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_dbs")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_dbs?q=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 412, "creating it again is 412: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"file_exists\"", "file_exists")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /tcae_dbs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"db_name\":\"tcae_dbs\"", "its name")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"doc_count\":0", "empty")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"cluster\":{\"q\":1", "one shard")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/_all_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET /_all_dbs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"tcae_dbs\"", "listed")
            sec = "{\"admins\":{\"names\":[],\"roles\":[]},\"members\":{\"names\":[],\"roles\":[\"readers\"]}}"
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_dbs/_security", sec)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "PUT _security: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_dbs/_security", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET _security: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"roles\":[\"readers\"]", "the members' role")
            delete_db("tcae_dbs")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"reason\":\"Database does not exist.\"", "does not exist")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "deleting it again is 404: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: one document's life, in tcae_crud.
        //   PUT    /tcae_crud/apple {"type":"fruit","name":"apple","price":3} -> 201 {"ok":true,"id":"apple","rev":"1-..."}
        //   GET    /tcae_crud/apple -> 200 the document with _id and _rev
        //   PUT    /tcae_crud/apple {"_rev":<rev 1>,...,"price":4} -> 201 rev "2-..."
        //   GET    /tcae_crud/apple?revs_info=true -> 200, _revs_info: both revs "available"
        //   GET    /tcae_crud/apple?rev=<rev 1> -> 200 the old revision (price 3), until compaction
        //   DELETE /tcae_crud/apple?rev=<rev 2> -> 200 {"ok":true,..,"rev":"3-..."}
        //   GET    /tcae_crud/apple -> 404 {"error":"not_found","reason":"deleted"}
        //   GET    /tcae_crud/pear  -> 404 {"error":"not_found","reason":"missing"}
        // The revs are deterministic (see the header), so the tape's revs
        // are what a port's CouchDB would answer too; the test still takes
        // each rev from the previous response, as a client must.
        spec.it("creates, reads, updates and deletes a document") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_reads_updates_and_deletes_a_document", "tcae_crud")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_crud")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_crud/apple", "{\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"apple\",\"price\":3}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "PUT a new document: ${b}")
            rev1 = jstr(b, "rev")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(rev1, "1-") == 1, "its first rev: ${rev1}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_crud/apple", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET it: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"_id\":\"apple\",\"_rev\":\"${rev1}\",\"type\":\"fruit\"", "id, rev, then its fields")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_crud/apple", "{\"_rev\":\"${rev1}\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"apple\",\"price\":4}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "update with the current rev: ${b}")
            rev2 = jstr(b, "rev")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(rev2, "2-") == 1, "a second rev: ${rev2}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_crud/apple?revs_info=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET ?revs_info=true: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"_revs_info\":[{\"rev\":\"${rev2}\",\"status\":\"available\"},{\"rev\":\"${rev1}\",\"status\":\"available\"}]", "both revs")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_crud/apple?rev=${rev1}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET the old rev: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"price\":3", "the old content")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_crud/apple?rev=${rev2}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "DELETE with the current rev: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(jstr(b, "rev"), "3-") == 1, "a deletion is a third rev")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_crud/apple", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a deleted document: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"reason\":\"deleted\"", "reason deleted")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_crud/pear", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a document never written: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"reason\":\"missing\"", "reason missing")
            delete_db("tcae_crud")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: optimistic concurrency, in tcae_conflict409.
        //   PUT    /tcae_conflict409/doc {"v":1}            -> 201 rev 1
        //   PUT    /tcae_conflict409/doc {"v":1}            -> 409 {"error":"conflict","reason":"Document update conflict."}  (no _rev)
        //   PUT    /tcae_conflict409/doc {"_rev":<1>,"v":2} -> 201 rev 2
        //   PUT    /tcae_conflict409/doc {"_rev":<1>,"v":3} -> 409 (stale rev)
        //   DELETE /tcae_conflict409/doc?rev=<1>            -> 409 (stale rev)
        //   GET    /tcae_conflict409/doc                    -> 200, still v 2
        spec.it("refuses a stale revision with a 409") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("refuses_a_stale_revision_with_a_409", "tcae_conflict409")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_conflict409")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_conflict409/doc", "{\"v\":1}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "created: ${b}")
            rev1 = jstr(b, "rev")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_conflict409/doc", "{\"v\":1}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "a write without the rev: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"error\":\"conflict\",\"reason\":\"Document update conflict.\"}", "conflict")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_conflict409/doc", "{\"_rev\":\"${rev1}\",\"v\":2}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "with the current rev: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_conflict409/doc", "{\"_rev\":\"${rev1}\",\"v\":3}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "with a stale rev: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_conflict409/doc?rev=${rev1}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "delete with a stale rev: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_conflict409/doc", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"v\":2", "the second write stands")
            delete_db("tcae_conflict409")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a replication-style conflict, in tcae_conflicts. Two
        // first revisions of one document written as a replicator would,
        // with their revs given and new_edits=false (no 409: both are kept).
        //   POST   /tcae_conflicts/_bulk_docs {"new_edits":false,"docs":[
        //            {"_id":"doc","_rev":"1-aaaa...","side":"a"},
        //            {"_id":"doc","_rev":"1-bbbb...","side":"b"}]} -> 201 []
        //   GET    /tcae_conflicts/doc?conflicts=true -> 200: the winner
        //          (the higher rev, 1-bbbb..., side b) and "_conflicts":["1-aaaa..."]
        //   DELETE /tcae_conflicts/doc?rev=1-aaaa... -> 200 (resolve: delete the loser)
        //   GET    /tcae_conflicts/doc?conflicts=true -> 200, no _conflicts
        spec.it("keeps both sides of a replication conflict until resolved") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("keeps_both_sides_of_a_replication_conflict_until_resolved", "tcae_conflicts")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_conflicts")
            ra = "1-aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
            rb = "1-bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_conflicts/_bulk_docs", "{\"new_edits\":false,\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"doc\",\"_rev\":\"${ra}\",\"side\":\"a\"},{\"_id\":\"doc\",\"_rev\":\"${rb}\",\"side\":\"b\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "both written: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_conflicts/doc?conflicts=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET ?conflicts=true: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"_rev\":\"${rb}\",\"side\":\"b\"", "the higher rev wins")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"_conflicts\":[\"${ra}\"]", "the other is a conflict")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_conflicts/doc?rev=${ra}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete the losing rev: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_conflicts/doc?conflicts=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET again: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.index_of(b, "_conflicts") < 0, "resolved: ${b}")
            delete_db("tcae_conflicts")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: _bulk_docs, in tcae_bulk. Always 201; each document's
        // outcome is in the array, in request order.
        //   POST /tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs {"docs":[{"_id":"a","n":1},{"_id":"b","n":2},{"_id":"c","n":3}]}
        //        -> 201 [{"ok":true,"id":"a","rev":"1-.."},..]
        //   POST /tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs {"docs":[{"_id":"a","_rev":<a's>,"n":10},{"_id":"b","n":20}]}
        //        -> 201 [{"ok":true,"id":"a","rev":"2-.."},{"id":"b","error":"conflict","reason":"Document update conflict."}]
        //   POST /tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs {"docs":[{"_id":"c","_rev":<c's>,"_deleted":true}]} -> 201, c deleted
        //   GET  /tcae_bulk -> 200, doc_count 2, doc_del_count 1
        spec.it("writes documents in bulk") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("writes_documents_in_bulk", "tcae_bulk")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_bulk")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"a\",\"n\":1},{\"_id\":\"b\",\"n\":2},{\"_id\":\"c\",\"n\":3}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "three created: ${b}")
            ra = jstr(b, "0.rev")
            rc = jstr(b, "2.rev")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(ra, "1-") == 1, "a's rev")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"a\",\"_rev\":\"${ra}\",\"n\":10},{\"_id\":\"b\",\"n\":20}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "a mixed batch is still 201: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(jstr(b, "0.rev"), "2-") == 1, "a updated")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"id\":\"b\",\"error\":\"conflict\",\"reason\":\"Document update conflict.\"}", "b refused, alone")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_bulk/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"c\",\"_rev\":\"${rc}\",\"_deleted\":true}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "c deleted: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_bulk", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"doc_del_count\":1,\"doc_count\":2", "two left, one deleted")
            delete_db("tcae_bulk")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: _all_docs, in tcae_alldocs, over five documents a..e
        // written with _bulk_docs. Keys are JSON in the query string,
        // percent-encoded ("b" is %22b%22). Rows are sorted by _id.
        //   GET  /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs                          -> total_rows 5, rows a..e (id, key, value.rev)
        //   GET  /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?include_docs=true&limit=2 -> a, b with "doc"
        //   GET  /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?startkey=%22b%22&endkey=%22d%22 -> b, c, d (endkey inclusive)
        //   GET  /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?descending=true&limit=2&skip=1 -> d, c
        //   GET  /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?key=%22c%22               -> c
        //   POST /tcae_alldocs/_all_docs {"keys":["e","nope","a"]} -> e, {"key":"nope","error":"not_found"}, a
        spec.it("lists documents with _all_docs and its parameters") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("lists_documents_with_all_docs_and_its_parameters", "tcae_alldocs")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_alldocs")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_alldocs/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"a\",\"n\":1},{\"_id\":\"b\",\"n\":2},{\"_id\":\"c\",\"n\":3},{\"_id\":\"d\",\"n\":4},{\"_id\":\"e\",\"n\":5}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "five documents: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_all_docs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"total_rows\":5", "five rows")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "rows.4.id"), "e", "sorted by id")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?include_docs=true&limit=2", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "include_docs, limit: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"doc\":{\"_id\":\"b\"", "the documents themselves")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "rows.2.id"), "", "two rows")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?startkey=${qk("b")}&endkey=${qk("d")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a key range: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.2.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.3.id")}", "bcd", "b to d, inclusive")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?descending=true&limit=2&skip=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "descending, skip, limit: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.id")}", "dc", "d then c")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs?key=${qk("c")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "one key: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.id")}", "c", "just c")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_alldocs/_all_docs", "{\"keys\":[\"e\",\"nope\",\"a\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "POST keys: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"key\":\"nope\",\"error\":\"not_found\"}", "a missing key is a row with an error")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}|${jstr(b, "rows.2.id")}", "e|a", "in the order asked")
            delete_db("tcae_alldocs")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a standalone attachment, in tcae_att. The upload's body is
        // the raw bytes with their own Content-Type, not JSON.
        //   PUT    /tcae_att/doc {"title":"with a note"}                -> 201 rev 1
        //   PUT    /tcae_att/doc/note.txt?rev=<1>  (text/plain) hello attachments -> 201 rev 2
        //   GET    /tcae_att/doc/note.txt -> 200 text/plain, the bytes, ETag "<base64 md5>"
        //   GET    /tcae_att/doc          -> 200, _attachments.note.txt stub: content_type,
        //                                    revpos 2, digest "md5-...", length 17, "stub":true
        //   DELETE /tcae_att/doc/note.txt?rev=<2> -> 200 rev 3
        //   GET    /tcae_att/doc/note.txt -> 404 {"error":"not_found",..}
        spec.it("stores and serves a standalone attachment") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("stores_and_serves_a_standalone_attachment", "tcae_att")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_att")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_att/doc", "{\"title\":\"with a note\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "the document: ${b}")
            rev1 = jstr(b, "rev")
            st, b = couch_typed("PUT", "/tcae_att/doc/note.txt?rev=${rev1}", "text/plain", "hello attachments")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "the attachment: ${b}")
            rev2 = jstr(b, "rev")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(rev2, "2-") == 1, "an attachment makes a new rev")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_att/doc/note.txt", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET the attachment: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "hello attachments", "its bytes")
            spec.assert_str_eq(last_content_type, "text/plain", "its content type")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(last_etag) > 0, "an ETag: ${last_etag}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_att/doc", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET the document: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"note.txt\":{\"content_type\":\"text/plain\",\"revpos\":2,\"digest\":\"md5-", "a stub")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"length\":17,\"stub\":true", "its length")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_att/doc/note.txt?rev=${rev2}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "DELETE the attachment: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_att/doc/note.txt", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            delete_db("tcae_att")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: an inline attachment, in tcae_inline: base64 in the
        // document's _attachments, in the same PUT.
        //   PUT /tcae_inline/doc {"title":"inline","_attachments":{"hello.txt":
        //        {"content_type":"text/plain","data":"aGVsbG8gd29ybGQ="}}} -> 201
        //   GET /tcae_inline/doc                    -> 200, a stub (length 11, no data)
        //   GET /tcae_inline/doc?attachments=true   -> 200, "data":"aGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=" inline
        //       (sent with `Accept: application/json`: without it CouchDB
        //       answers multipart/related with the attachment gzipped)
        //   GET /tcae_inline/doc/hello.txt          -> 200 text/plain "hello world"
        spec.it("stores an inline attachment and reads it back with the document") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("stores_an_inline_attachment_and_reads_it_back_with_the_document", "tcae_inline")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_inline")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_inline/doc", "{\"title\":\"inline\",\"_attachments\":{\"hello.txt\":{\"content_type\":\"text/plain\",\"data\":\"aGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=\"}}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "document and attachment in one PUT: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_inline/doc", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"length\":11,\"stub\":true", "a stub by default")
            st, b = couch_json("/tcae_inline/doc?attachments=true")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET ?attachments=true: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"data\":\"aGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=\"", "the bytes inline, base64")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_inline/doc/hello.txt", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET the attachment: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "hello world", "decoded")
            delete_db("tcae_inline")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a design document and its views, in tcae_views. Five
        // products (type, name, price) by _bulk_docs, then
        //   PUT /tcae_views/_design/shop {"language":"javascript","views":{
        //        "by_type":{"map":"function (doc) { if (doc.type) emit(doc.type, doc.price); }","reduce":"_sum"},
        //        "by_name":{"map":"function (doc) { emit(doc.name, null); }","reduce":"_count"}}} -> 201
        //   GET /tcae_views/_design/shop                                -> 200, the design document
        //   GET .../_view/by_type                                      -> reduced: one row, key null, the total
        //   GET .../_view/by_type?group=true                           -> a row per type with its sum
        //   GET .../_view/by_type?reduce=false                         -> the map rows, sorted by key then id
        //   GET .../_view/by_type?reduce=false&key=%22fruit%22&include_docs=true -> the fruit, with docs
        //   GET .../_view/by_name?reduce=false&startkey=%22b%22&endkey=%22d%22   -> a key range
        //   GET .../_view/by_name?reduce=false&descending=true&limit=2           -> the last two names
        //   POST .../_view/by_type {"keys":["veg"],"reduce":false}      -> rows for those keys
        // The first query builds the index; the answer still comes back in
        // the one response, so nothing is polled.
        spec.it("queries a map reduce view") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("queries_a_map_reduce_view", "tcae_views")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_views")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_views/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"p1\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"apple\",\"price\":3},{\"_id\":\"p2\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"banana\",\"price\":2},{\"_id\":\"p3\",\"type\":\"veg\",\"name\":\"carrot\",\"price\":1},{\"_id\":\"p4\",\"type\":\"veg\",\"name\":\"daikon\",\"price\":4},{\"_id\":\"p5\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"elderberry\",\"price\":5}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "five products: ${b}")
            ddoc = "{\"language\":\"javascript\",\"views\":{\"by_type\":{\"map\":\"function (doc) { if (doc.type) emit(doc.type, doc.price); }\",\"reduce\":\"_sum\"},\"by_name\":{\"map\":\"function (doc) { emit(doc.name, null); }\",\"reduce\":\"_count\"}}}"
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_views/_design/shop", ddoc)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "the design document: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"id\":\"_design/shop\"", "its id")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_views/_design/shop", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET it back: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"reduce\":\"_sum\"", "the views")
            v = "/tcae_views/_design/shop/_view"
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_type", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "reduced: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "{\"rows\":[\n{\"key\":null,\"value\":15}\n]}", "the sum of all prices")
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_type?group=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "grouped: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "{\"key\":\"fruit\",\"value\":10},\n{\"key\":\"veg\",\"value\":5}", "per type")
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_type?reduce=false", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "map rows: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"total_rows\":5", "five rows")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"id\":\"p1\",\"key\":\"fruit\",\"value\":3}", "id, key and value")
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_type?reduce=false&key=${qk("fruit")}&include_docs=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "one key with docs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.2.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.3.id")}", "p1p2p5", "the three fruit")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"doc\":{\"_id\":\"p5\"", "with their documents")
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_name?reduce=false&startkey=${qk("b")}&endkey=${qk("d")}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a key range: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.key")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.key")}${jstr(b, "rows.2.key")}", "bananacarrot", "names from b up to d (daikon > d)")
            st, b = couch("GET", "${v}/by_name?reduce=false&descending=true&limit=2", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "descending, limit: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.key")},${jstr(b, "rows.1.key")}", "elderberry,daikon", "the last two")
            st, b = couch("POST", "${v}/by_type", "{\"keys\":[\"veg\"],\"reduce\":false}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "POST keys: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "rows.0.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.1.id")}${jstr(b, "rows.2.id")}", "p3p4", "the veg")
            delete_db("tcae_views")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: Mango, in tcae_mango, over the same five products.
        //   POST /tcae_mango/_find {"selector":{"price":{"$gt":2}},"fields":["_id","name"]}
        //        -> 200 docs p1, p4, p5, a "bookmark", and a "warning" (no index)
        //   POST /tcae_mango/_index {"index":{"fields":["type","price"]},"name":"type-price","ddoc":"mango-type-price","type":"json"}
        //        -> 200 {"result":"created","id":"_design/mango-type-price","name":"type-price"}
        //   POST /tcae_mango/_index (the same) -> 200 "result":"exists"
        //   GET  /tcae_mango/_index -> 200: _all_docs (special) and type-price
        //   POST /tcae_mango/_find {"selector":{"type":"fruit","price":{"$gte":2}},
        //        "sort":[{"type":"asc"},{"price":"asc"}],"fields":["name","price"],"limit":2}
        //        -> 200 banana 2, apple 3; no warning (the index serves it)
        //   POST /tcae_mango/_find {"selector":{"type":"fruit","price":{"$gte":2}},
        //        "sort":[{"type":"asc"},{"price":"asc"}],"fields":["name","price"],"limit":2,"bookmark":<from before>}
        //        -> 200 the next page: elderberry 5
        //   DELETE /tcae_mango/_index/_design/mango-type-price/json/type-price -> 200 {"ok":true}
        // Bookmarks are opaque but deterministic: the same on every run.
        spec.it("finds documents with mango and an index") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("finds_documents_with_mango_and_an_index", "tcae_mango")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_mango")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"p1\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"apple\",\"price\":3},{\"_id\":\"p2\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"banana\",\"price\":2},{\"_id\":\"p3\",\"type\":\"veg\",\"name\":\"carrot\",\"price\":1},{\"_id\":\"p4\",\"type\":\"veg\",\"name\":\"daikon\",\"price\":4},{\"_id\":\"p5\",\"type\":\"fruit\",\"name\":\"elderberry\",\"price\":5}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "five products: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_find", "{\"selector\":{\"price\":{\"$gt\":2}},\"fields\":[\"_id\",\"name\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_find with no index: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "docs.0._id")}${jstr(b, "docs.1._id")}${jstr(b, "docs.2._id")}", "p1p4p5", "price > 2")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"warning\":", "a warning that no index matched")
            idx = "{\"index\":{\"fields\":[\"type\",\"price\"]},\"name\":\"type-price\",\"ddoc\":\"mango-type-price\",\"type\":\"json\"}"
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_index", idx)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create an index: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"result\":\"created\"", "created")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_index", idx)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the same again: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"result\":\"exists\"", "exists")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_mango/_index", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list indexes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"total_rows\":2", "_all_docs and ours")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ddoc\":\"_design/mango-type-price\",\"name\":\"type-price\"", "ours")
            query = "\"selector\":{\"type\":\"fruit\",\"price\":{\"$gte\":2}},\"sort\":[{\"type\":\"asc\"},{\"price\":\"asc\"}],\"fields\":[\"name\",\"price\"],\"limit\":2"
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_find", "{${query}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_find, sorted by the index: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "{\"name\":\"banana\",\"price\":2},\n{\"name\":\"apple\",\"price\":3}", "cheapest fruit first, two of them")
            spec.assert_true(string.index_of(b, "warning") < 0, "no warning: the index served it")
            bookmark = jstr(b, "bookmark")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(bookmark) > 0, "a bookmark")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_mango/_find", "{${query},\"bookmark\":\"${bookmark}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the next page: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"name\":\"elderberry\",\"price\":5}", "the rest")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_mango/_index/_design/mango-type-price/json/type-price", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete the index: ${b}")
            delete_db("tcae_mango")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the changes feed (feed=normal, the default: one response,
        // then done), in tcae_changes. Sequence ids are opaque strings, on
        // the tape as {{seq-N}}; a client stores last_seq and sends it back.
        //   POST /tcae_changes/_bulk_docs {"docs":[{"_id":"a","v":1},{"_id":"b","v":1}]}
        //   GET  /tcae_changes/_changes -> 200 results a, b (seq, id, changes[{rev}]), last_seq, pending 0
        //   PUT  /tcae_changes/c {"v":1}; PUT /tcae_changes/a {"_rev":..,"v":2}
        //   GET  /tcae_changes/_changes?since=<last_seq> -> only c and a
        //   DELETE /tcae_changes/b?rev=..
        //   GET  /tcae_changes/_changes?since=<last_seq 2>&include_docs=true -> b, "deleted":true, with its doc
        //   GET  /tcae_changes/_changes?limit=1 -> one result, "pending":2
        spec.it("follows the changes feed with since") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("follows_the_changes_feed_with_since", "tcae_changes")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_changes")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_changes/_bulk_docs", "{\"docs\":[{\"_id\":\"a\",\"v\":1},{\"_id\":\"b\",\"v\":1}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "two documents: ${b}")
            ra = jstr(b, "0.rev")
            rb = jstr(b, "1.rev")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_changes/_changes", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_changes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "results.0.id")}${jstr(b, "results.1.id")}", "ab", "both, in write order")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"pending\":0", "nothing pending")
            since1 = jstr(b, "last_seq")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(since1) > 0, "a last_seq")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_changes/c", "{\"v\":1}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "c: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_changes/a", "{\"_rev\":\"${ra}\",\"v\":2}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "a again: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_changes/_changes?since=${since1}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_changes since: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq("${jstr(b, "results.0.id")}${jstr(b, "results.1.id")}${jstr(b, "results.2.id")}", "ca", "only what changed since, c then a")
            since2 = jstr(b, "last_seq")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_changes/b?rev=${rb}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "b deleted: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_changes/_changes?since=${since2}&include_docs=true", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_changes since, with docs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"id\":\"b\"", "b")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"deleted\":true", "as a deletion")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"doc\":{\"_id\":\"b\"", "with its (tombstone) doc")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_changes/_changes?limit=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_changes limit: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"pending\":2", "two more to come")
            delete_db("tcae_changes")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: ids minted by the server, in tcae_ids. The 32-hex ids are
        // {{uuid-N}} on the tape, the same token in the later request paths,
        // so a port reads them from the response as a client would.
        //   GET  /_uuids?count=1   -> 200 {"uuids":["{{uuid-1}}"]}
        //   PUT  /tcae_ids/{{uuid-1}} {"from":"_uuids"} -> 201
        //   POST /tcae_ids {"from":"post"} -> 201 {"ok":true,"id":"{{uuid-2}}","rev":..}, Location header
        //   GET  /tcae_ids/{{uuid-2}} -> 200
        //   GET  /tcae_ids/_all_docs -> 200, both ids
        spec.it("creates documents under server generated ids") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_documents_under_server_generated_ids", "tcae_ids")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            create_db("tcae_ids")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/_uuids?count=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a uuid: ${b}")
            u = jstr(b, "uuids.0")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(u) > 0, "a uuid: ${u}")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_ids/${u}", "{\"from\":\"_uuids\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "PUT under it: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_ids", "{\"from\":\"post\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 201, "POST without an id: ${b}")
            id = jstr(b, "id")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(id) > 0, "the server picked an id: ${id}")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_ids/${id}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET it: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"from\":\"post\"", "the document")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_ids/_all_docs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "_all_docs: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"total_rows\":2", "both")
            delete_db("tcae_ids")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the error statuses a client must handle (401 is in
        // refuses_a_client_that_has_not_logged_in, 409 in the two conflict
        // tapes). Every error body is {"error":<kind>,"reason":<text>}.
        //   GET    /tcae_nosuch          -> 404 not_found "Database does not exist."
        //   PUT    /Bad_Name             -> 400 illegal_database_name (lower case first)
        //   PUT    /tcae_errors?q=1      -> 201;  again -> 412 file_exists
        //   GET    /tcae_errors/nope     -> 404 not_found "missing"
        //   PUT    /tcae_errors/_nope {} -> 400 illegal_docid (ids starting "_" are reserved)
        //   POST   /tcae_errors {not json -> 400 bad_request
        //   DELETE /tcae_errors/nope?rev=1-0123... -> 404 not_found
        //   DELETE /_all_dbs             -> 405 method_not_allowed
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses", "tcae_errors")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a missing database: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"error\":\"not_found\",\"reason\":\"Database does not exist.\"}", "not_found")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/Bad_Name", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an illegal database name: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"illegal_database_name\"", "illegal_database_name")
            create_db("tcae_errors")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_errors?q=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 412, "an existing database: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"file_exists\"", "file_exists")
            st, b = couch("GET", "/tcae_errors/nope", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a missing document: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "{\"error\":\"not_found\",\"reason\":\"missing\"}", "missing")
            st, b = couch("PUT", "/tcae_errors/_nope", "{}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a reserved id: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"illegal_docid\"", "illegal_docid")
            st, b = couch("POST", "/tcae_errors", "{not json")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a body that is not JSON: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"bad_request\"", "bad_request")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/tcae_errors/nope?rev=1-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "deleting a missing document: ${b}")
            st, b = couch("DELETE", "/_all_dbs", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 405, "a method the endpoint does not take: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"method_not_allowed\"", "method_not_allowed")
            delete_db("tcae_errors")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("couchdb: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
